@startuml
!include_once ../docs/images/common-component.iuml

title Receiver — MLAT Provider Topology

component "Receiver\n--\nTags: raw, icao_hex, received_at, source" as Receiver $OnPrem

component "MLAT Provider A\n(e.g. mlat-client feed)" as MlatA $Vendor
component "MLAT Provider B\n(e.g. a different aggregator)" as MlatB $Vendor

Receiver -up-> MlatA : TCP Socket\nPort 30105
Receiver -up-> MlatB : TCP Socket\nPort 30106

note bottom of MlatB
    Any number of MLAT providers can be configured — each is its own
    ""sources[]"" entry with ""source: "MLAT""", a plain TCP connection
    like any other source. MLAT providers are not co-located with the
    receiver's on-prem SDR hardware (see receiver.puml).
end note

@enduml
